# Git

Do **not** commit, push, or open a PR unless EsrgaN explicitly asks.

- Base branch: `main`. Never commit or push to `main`.
- Branches: `feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `docs/`, `test/`, `refactor/` + kebab-case English.
- Conventional Commits, English, why in the body:

```
feat: enqueue notifications before returning 202

Keep the HTTP path free of provider I/O so clients
get a stable notification_id under load.
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`, `refactor`, `chore`, `ci`.

- One concern per commit. Never commit `.env` or secrets.
- No `--no-verify`, no force-push to `main`, no interactive git (`-i`).
- PRs via `gh pr create` with Summary (what + why) and Test plan.
